            <ArticleTitle>Conservative treatment of Morton's neuroma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>343-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Morton's metatarsalgia (plantar digital neuritis) is a syndrome caused by the development of a neuroma in a digital nerve just proximal to its point of bifurcation. Severe neuralgic pain in the distal part of the sole is referred to the corresponding two toes. The treatment of this syndrome with the injection of a local anesthetic and methylprednisolone is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
